---
import Section from './Section.astro';
// Personal science — FDR-validated correlations + personal cutoffs. §1 calls this
// "a rigor most consumer apps don't attempt." The caffeine-cutoff example is from §1.
// Benjamini–Hochberg FDR control is footnoted to its primary source.
---

<Section
  n="08"
  id="personal"
  labelledby="personal-h"
  note="Detection is free, shown as plain statistics. The coach that explains and acts on it is the premium layer — PRICING.md §1a."
>
  <p class="eyebrow rise">Personal science</p>
  <h2 id="personal-h" class="rise mt-4 max-w-2xl text-[clamp(1.9rem,4vw,2.9rem)]">
    Findings from <span class="italic text-accent-soft">your</span> data &mdash; corrected for
    chance.
  </h2>

  <div class="mt-10 grid items-center gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1fr] lg:gap-16">
    <div class="rise">
      <p class="lede">
        Robust per-metric baselines, anomaly flags, and correlations tested with Spearman and
        Mann&ndash;Whitney under Benjamini&ndash;Hochberg false-discovery-rate control<sup class="ref"
          ><a href="#ref-5" aria-label="reference 5">5</a></sup
        > &mdash; so a &ldquo;finding&rdquo; has survived the multiple-comparisons problem, not just
        caught your eye on a chart.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-5 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-faint">
        It&rsquo;s a rigor most consumer apps don&rsquo;t attempt. And a pattern in your own data is
        the strongest motivator there is &mdash; because it&rsquo;s yours, not a study&rsquo;s.
      </p>
    </div>

    <figure
      class="surface rise p-6 sm:p-7"
      aria-label="Rendered example: an FDR-controlled personal finding about late caffeine"
    >
      <figcaption class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
        <span class="mono text-[0.66rem] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-ink-faint">
          Personal finding &middot; validated
        </span>
        <span class="chip chip-gold chip-dot">FDR-controlled</span>
      </figcaption>
      <hr class="hairline my-5" />
      <p class="font-serif text-[1.6rem] leading-snug">
        Caffeine after <span class="mono">~15:00</span>
        <span class="text-ink-faint">&rarr;</span>
        <span class="text-accent-soft">&minus;40 min</span> sleep
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[0.92rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        On nights you logged a late coffee, you slept about 40 minutes less. Tested against your own
        baseline &mdash; a pattern in your data, never a population average pinned onto you.
      </p>
      <dl class="mono mt-5 grid grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-x-4 gap-y-1.5 text-xs text-ink-faint">
        <dt>test</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Mann&ndash;Whitney, BH-corrected</dd>
        <dt>window</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">60 days</dd>
        <dt>holds</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">after correcting for chance</dd>
      </dl>
    </figure>
  </div>
</Section>
